Package: batchit
Title: Run One R Function Across Many Worker Processes
Version: 26.8.6
Authors@R: person(c("Richard","Aubrey"), "White", email = "hello@rwhite.no", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6747-1726"))
Description: Runs one R function once per item in a list of inputs, each call in
    its own worker process. Return values come back as a list, or are discarded
    when the function is called for a side effect, or the function's declared
    output files are written for it. Naming the function by package and symbol
    rather than passing it by value lets a worker hash what it loaded and refuse
    code that differs from what was dispatched. Every item's arguments are
    checked against the function's formals in both the calling session and the
    worker. Warnings raised by an item that completes are carried back and
    re-raised in the calling session, labelled with that item, while an item
    that fails stops the call rather than returning a partial result. Output files are staged
    beside their destinations and renamed into place, so a failed item leaves no
    half-written file. Two transports are available: a fresh process per item via 'processx',
    where process exit is what reclaims memory, and a lazy producer with bounded
    backpressure via 'mirai' daemons for items that must be generated on demand.
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
